From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:31:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 116/274] TileLang V4.1 WO: WO-A in four K shards, split over
 CTAs at decode

At decode WO-A's 64-tile grid left SMs idle (about 400 GB/s against B12X's
fused WO near 720; the whole WO 1.2-1.4x B12X up to 96 rows). The W8A16 GEMM now
sums K in four shards at every row count, each from zero, added in shard order:
decode rows (up to 128) give each shard its own CTA, FP32 partials then
splitk_reduce; longer steps add the shards inside the kernel (the bf16_gemm
pattern). A row's bits therefore do not depend on the path, which the WO-A test
checks across the split and in-kernel row counts.

(cherry picked from commit cec0da371684077e933a957614fcfb7f38ddcca8)

